{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KxiJ4S1ipcNL5Rvu5VWFAy","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on the context filesystem, here is the information about Sahil Devgon's Apache Kafka discussion on KIP-1291:\\\\n\\\\n## Apache Kafka Mailing List Discussion - KIP-1291: Extended I/O Metrics Collection\\\\n\\\\n**From `/store/discussions/kip-1291-extended-io-metrics.md`:**\\\\n\\\\n- **KIP**: KIP-1291 - Extended I/O Metrics Collection\\\\n- **Status**: Discussion Started\\\\n- **Proposal URL**: https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/x/co48G\\\\n- **Started by**: Sahil Devgon\\\\n- **Started Date**: February 25, 2026 (14:50:44 UTC)\\\\n- **Mailing List**: dev@kafka.apache.org\\\\n- **Thread ID**: CAD38bmS_TiDq6cTxse3ecYV+vOZ2oX6gthDEc-dgC-q-p-Sg=g@mail.gmail.com\\\\n\\\\n**Proposal Overview:**\\\\nThe KIP extends I/O metrics collection to expose all 7 Linux I/O metrics from `/proc/self/io` instead of just the current 2 (read_bytes and write_bytes). The 5 additional metrics proposed are:\\\\n- rchar (read characters)\\\\n- wchar (write characters)\\\\n- syscr (system calls read)\\\\n- syscw (system calls write)\\\\n- cancelled_write_bytes\\\\n\\\\nThese metrics enable operators to diagnose cache effectiveness, measure write amplification, and identify I/O pattern inefficiencies.\\\\n\\\\n## Related JIRA Issue\\\\n\\\\n**From `/store/issues/kafka-20223-extended-io-metrics.md`:**\\\\n\\\\n- **Issue**: KAFKA-20223\\\\n- **Status**: Open\\\\n- **Priority**: Minor\\\\n- **Reporter**: Sahil Devgon\\\\n- **Created**: February 25, 2026 (14:17:45 UTC)\\\\n- **Description**: Extended I/O Metrics Collection for KIP-1291, with implementation details at https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/x/co48G\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"discussions/kip-1291-extended-io-metrics.md\\\",\\\"issues/kafka-20223-extended-io-metrics.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":11.69,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":2,\\\"us